# Valgrind suppressions for the dartunifrac C harness.
#
# One, and only what the harness has been seen to need (`valgrind -s` lists
# which suppressions matched). A dedicated rayon pool is not joined when it is
# dropped: its threads are told to stop and exit on their own, so threads still
# running when the process ends leave glibc's per-thread TLS block "possibly
# lost". Anchoring on pthread_create keeps this narrow: our code never creates a
# thread, so no block allocated by our own code can match, even when that code
# runs on a pool worker.
#
# Deliberately not suppressed: the pool's registry, which is "still reachable"
# for the same reason. That kind is not an error, so the gate passes without
# hiding anything. sc's broader rayon/crossbeam patterns are left out for the
# same reason; add one only when `valgrind -s` shows it matching a specific
# block.

{
   rayon-pool-thread-tls
   Memcheck:Leak
   match-leak-kinds: possible
   ...
   fun:pthread_create*
}
